    "shot": "hero",
    "source": "\n**Frame:** A named investigator's published caution, set as text on a screen with its byline\nand date visible, in the register the critic's window uses. No face, no body, no room.\n\n**Screen / system text — PUBLISHED, ATTRIBUTED (PARAPHRASED):**\n`SOME OF THE INCENTIVES ON A THIRD-PARTY INVESTIGATOR PUSH TOWARD MAXIMIZING THE APPEARANCE\nOF ASSURANCE WITHOUT PROVIDING MEANINGFUL OVERSIGHT.`\n\n**Action:** The strongest warning about the investigation comes from inside it.\n\n**Provenance:** `documented` — attributed paraphrase of Beth Barnes' dated public writing,\nregistered in [`sources.md`](../../research/sources.md). She is describing the position of a\nthird-party investigator, not this book, and the page may not extend it to anyone she did\nnot name.\n\n",
    "title": "A published caution appears only as attributed text"
  }
